    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0137" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">555.E1/14a: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Diplomatic Representatives in All
                        Countries</hi><anchor n="27" xml:id="d47-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>You are instructed to deliver the following invitation in the name of the
                    President to the government to which you are accredited: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The President of the United States in accordance with the provisions of
                            Part XIII of the Treaty of Peace between the Allied and Associated
                            Powers and Germany signed at Versailles on June 28, 1919 and under
                            authority vested in him by Congress,<anchor n="28" xml:id="d47-f2"/>
                            hereby convenes <pb facs="0138" n="36" xml:id="pg36"/> the first meeting
                            of the Annual Labor Conference therein described to assemble in
                            Washington at noon on the 29th day of October, 1919.</p>
                        <p>The Government of the United States extends to each nation which is or
                            which prior to the said meeting shall become a member of the
                            International Labor Organization as defined in Article 387 an invitation
                            to send its delegates and other representatives to Washington for the
                            purpose of attending such conference.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>You will also inform the government to which you are accredited that all details
                    as to reception of and accommodations for its representatives in Washington may
                    be arranged through its diplomatic representative here.<anchor n="29"
                        xml:id="d47-f3"/> Please obtain and telegraph to the Department the names of
                    the delegates and their advisers. The cost of all telegrams should be stated
                    therein in order that the Department may obtain reimbursement.</p>
                <p>You will also offer your aid in the matter of passports, transportation etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d47-f1" n="27" type="source" xml:id="d47-f1-content">
                <p>Except those in Mexico, Russia, and the Dominican Republic.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d47-f2" n="28" xml:id="d47-f2-content">
                <p>41 Stat. 279.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d47-f3" n="29" xml:id="d47-f3-content">
                <p>In telegrams to the representatives in Poland and Liberia this phrase reads
                    “through you”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
